      "text": "The problem states that the set of three numbers has both a mean and median equal to 4. Let's denote the three numbers in ascending order as \\(a, b, c\\), where \\(a \\leq b \\leq c\\). Given \\(a = 1\\), the median of the set is \\(b = 4\\). The mean of the set is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a + b + c}{3} = 4\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(a = 1\\) and \\(b = 4\\) into the equation, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1 + 4 + c}{3} = 4\n\\]\n\nSimplifying this equation, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{5 + c}{3} = 4\n\\]\n\nMultiplying both sides by 3 to clear the fraction, we get:\n\n\\[\n5 + c = 12\n\\]\n\nSubtracting 5 from both sides, we find:\n\n\\[\nc = 7\n\\]\n\nThus, the three numbers in ascending order are \\(1, 4, 7\\). The range of the set is the difference between the largest and smallest numbers:\n\n\\[\nc - a = 7 - 1 = 6\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the range of the set of numbers is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
